  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 16-layer alternating HfO2/SiO2 multilayer stack on fused silica substrate for dual-band performance. Layer sequence: HfO2/SiO2 repeated 8 times starting with HfO2 at air interface. Initialize all layer thicknesses with uniform random sampling within bounds: HfO2 layers 38-45 nm, SiO2 layers 47-55 nm (quarter-wave at 300 nm ±8%). Optimize thicknesses using gradient-based optimizer with Adam-LBFGS hybrid. Spectral evaluation: 200-1500 nm with 1 nm resolution. Objectives: maximize mean transmittance 800-1500 nm, maximize mean reflectance 200-400 nm. Total layer count fixed at 16. Material registry resolves HfO2 and SiO2 refractive indices. If best_target_score improvement < 1e-3 for 4 consecutive iterations, trigger Monte Carlo resampling of thickness initialization. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 200-400 nm, 800-1500 nm. soft objectives: High transmission in 800-1500 nm band; High reflection in 200-400 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: Low transmission in 200-400 nm band; Low reflection in 800-1500 nm band. manufacturing constraints: Total layers <= 30; Materials limited to HfO2 and SiO2.",
